# Issue #82: quest-advancing NPC-to-NPC conversations the importer used to drop.
# Each case stands in for the quest's earlier progress with setstage, puts the player where a player would be, and
# waits for the stage the conversation's last line sets. No NPC is moved or touched.

# TG04Mistake: Hlidara's HELLO "You are in good spirits today, milady" (INFO 0000A173) names only its speaker; Alessia
# Caro (the Countess) is named by the reply. Gate: stage 10-69 and Hlidara within 400 of the player. Hlidara's last
# line "Do not worry, milady..." (INFO 00035FBB) sets 50. tdetect stands in for the thief sneaking: without it the
# Count's guard arrests the player for trespassing and the arrest menu holds the game.
# In Leyawiin the two share a room only at dinner, 20-23 (LeyawiinCastleDinnerHlidara/Alessia); by day Hlidara has
# no package and the Countess holds audience at the throne. The TES4 runner has no `rest`, so GameHour stands in for
# the player waiting until evening by Hlidara's dining chair.
case tg04_hlidara_alessia
run
setstage TG04Mistake 10
set GameHour to 19.5
tdetect
approach HlidaraMothrilDiningChairRef
until 3000 GetStageDone TG04Mistake 50
end

# MQ15: Orthe's HELLO "What's going on here? Who's this?" (INFO 0003EAAA, sets 57) opens a conversation whose replies
# belong to MQConversations; Eldamil's last line "Of course, kynreeve." (INFO 0003EABD) sets 58. 20 (Paradise arrival,
# which enables Orthe and Eldamil), 50, 54 and 56 (the player plays Eldamil's prisoner) stand in for the quest so far.
# The player walks to Orthe and Eldamil's escort package brings him along, as in the quest. Orthe's own lair check
# force-greets the player; that greeting sets 51 and, once 57 is done, 58 as well (authored race).
case mq15_orthe_eldamil
run
setstage MQ15 20
setstage MQ15 50
setstage MQ15 54
setstage MQ15 56
approach EldamilRef
walk OrtheRef
hear 3600 OrtheRef Who's this
until 3600 GetStageDone MQ15 58
end
